# ELEVATE Project Rules

You are working on ELEVATE, a Student UI Design Competition platform. Follow these rules strictly.

## Architecture

- Use Next.js App Router with TypeScript strict mode
- Default to Server Components; add "use client" only when needed
- All Supabase access goes through `src/lib/supabase/` utilities
- Never import `@supabase/supabase-js` directly in components
- Run the dev server on port 3010

## Design System (Non-Negotiable)

- **NEVER create ad-hoc UI** — use components from `@/components/ui`
- **New components MUST be added to `/design-system` page first** before use elsewhere
- **NEVER use arbitrary colors** — use semantic tokens: `primary-*`, `text-primary`, `bg-surface`, `border-border`
- **NEVER use arbitrary spacing** — follow the 4px grid via Tailwind utilities
- **Match existing patterns** for shadows (`shadow-xs` through `shadow-xl`), radius (`rounded-lg`, `rounded-xl`), and transitions (200ms)
- Read `design.md` before making visual changes
- Read `context.md` before making architectural changes

## Component Rules

- Import UI from `@/components/ui` barrel export
- Use `cn()` from `@/lib/utils/cn` for conditional classes
- Use `lucide-react` for icons (already tree-shaken via next.config)
- Use `next/image` for all images with proper `sizes` attribute
- Upvote interactions MUST use `UpvoteButton` component
- Project displays MUST use `ProjectCard` component

## Performance

- Do NOT add unnecessary dependencies
- Prefer native HTML elements (`<dialog>`, `<details>`) over libraries
- Use dynamic imports for heavy client components
- Keep client component boundaries as small as possible
- Optimize images: AVIF/WebP, lazy loading, responsive sizes

## File Organization

```
New UI component  → src/components/ui/[name].tsx + export in index.ts + showcase in design-system
New page          → src/app/[route]/page.tsx
New API route     → src/app/api/[route]/route.ts
New type          → src/types/
New constant      → src/lib/constants/
New utility       → src/lib/utils/
```

## Naming Conventions

- Components: PascalCase files and exports
- Hooks: `use` prefix, camelCase
- Types: PascalCase interfaces
- CSS variables: kebab-case with semantic names

## Code Quality

- Run `npm run lint` and `npm run typecheck` before completing tasks
- Format with Prettier (tailwind plugin sorts classes)
- No `any` types unless absolutely necessary with comment
- Form inputs must have labels and error states

## What NOT To Do

- ❌ Duplicate UI patterns instead of extending design system
- ❌ Inline styles or CSS modules (use Tailwind)
- ❌ Hardcode colors like `#6a1b9a` (use `primary-*` tokens)
- ❌ Skip accessibility (labels, aria attributes, focus rings)
- ❌ Build backend logic without RLS policies
- ❌ Commit `.env` files or secrets
- ❌ Add UI libraries (Radix, MUI, Chakra, shadcn CLI additions without design system integration)

## Documentation

When making significant changes, update:
- `context.md` — architecture changes
- `design.md` — visual/token changes
- `project-requirements.md` — business logic changes

## Voting Domain Rules (Phase 2+)

- Enforce one vote per user at database level (`UNIQUE(user_id)`)
- Validate deadline server-side on all write operations
- Vote changes must be atomic (delete old + insert new in transaction)
- Use optimistic UI with rollback on API failure
